[{"id":"hayia-23-37-6","words":["verb:hayia"],"options":[{"bs":"i živimo","en":"and we live"},{"bs":"živite","en":"you (all) live"},{"bs":"živio je","en":"he/it lived"},{"bs":"i živi","en":"and he/it lives"}],"ref":"23:37","answerWord":"وَنَحْيَا","answerSound":"audio/aa76dc279d841495ef37.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"There is naught but our life of the world; we die and we live, and we shall not be raised (again).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"živjeti","en":"to live"},"passage":["إِنْ","هِىَ","إِلَّا","حَيَاتُنَا","ٱلدُّنْيَا","نَمُوتُ","وَنَحْيَا","وَمَا","نَحْنُ","بِمَبْعُوثِينَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"حَيِيَ"}},{"id":"hayia-7-25-2","words":["verb:hayia"],"options":[{"bs":"živite","en":"you (all) live"},{"bs":"i živi","en":"and he/it lives"},{"bs":"i živimo","en":"and we live"},{"bs":"živio je","en":"he/it lived"}],"ref":"7:25","answerWord":"تَحْيَوْنَ","answerSound":"audio/b3bf4e1240602af6bdb4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He said: There shall ye live, and there shall ye die, and thence shall ye be brought forth.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"živjeti","en":"to live"},"passage":["قَالَ","فِيهَا","تَحْيَوْنَ","وَفِيهَا","تَمُوتُونَ","وَمِنْهَا","تُخْرَجُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"حَيِيَ"}},{"id":"qallaba-24-44-0","words":["verb:qallaba"],"options":[{"bs":"smjenjuje","en":"(He) alternates"},{"bs":"i okrećemo ih","en":"and we turn them over"},{"bs":"i okrećemo","en":"and we turn"},{"bs":"i prevrtali su","en":"and they turned over"}],"ref":"24:44","answerWord":"يُقَلِّبُ","answerSound":"audio/15c0a641a11545233699.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah causeth the revolution of the day and the night. Lo! herein is indeed a lesson for those who see.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prevrtati, okretati","en":"to turn over, to turn about"},"passage":["يُقَلِّبُ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلَّيْلَ","وَٱلنَّهَارَ","إِنَّ","فِى","ذَٰلِكَ","لَعِبْرَةً","لِّأُو۟لِى","ٱلْأَبْصَٰرِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"قَلَّبَ"}},{"id":"qallaba-6-110-0","words":["verb:qallaba"],"options":[{"bs":"i okrećemo","en":"and we turn"},{"bs":"i prevrtali su","en":"and they turned over"},{"bs":"smjenjuje","en":"(He) alternates"},{"bs":"i okrećemo ih","en":"and we turn them over"}],"ref":"6:110","answerWord":"وَنُقَلِّبُ","answerSound":"audio/11a790f1b893d5c3fe78.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We confound their hearts and their eyes. As they believed not therein at the first, We let them wander blindly on in their contumacy.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prevrtati, okretati","en":"to turn over, to turn about"},"passage":["وَنُقَلِّبُ","أَفْـِٔدَتَهُمْ","وَأَبْصَٰرَهُمْ","كَمَا","لَمْ","يُؤْمِنُوا۟","بِهِۦٓ","أَوَّلَ","مَرَّةٍ","وَنَذَرُهُمْ","فِى","طُغْيَٰنِهِمْ","يَعْمَهُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"قَلَّبَ"}},{"id":"qallaba-9-48-5","words":["verb:qallaba"],"options":[{"bs":"i prevrtali su","en":"and they turned over"},{"bs":"i okrećemo","en":"and we turn"},{"bs":"i okrećemo ih","en":"and we turn them over"},{"bs":"smjenjuje","en":"(He) alternates"}],"ref":"9:48","answerWord":"وَقَلَّبُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/e4504d02656def945226.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Aforetime they sought to cause sedition and raised difficulties for thee till the Truth came and the decree of Allah was made manifest, though they were loth.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prevrtati, okretati","en":"to turn over, to turn about"},"passage":["لَقَدِ","ٱبْتَغَوُا۟","ٱلْفِتْنَةَ","مِن","قَبْلُ","وَقَلَّبُوا۟","لَكَ","ٱلْأُمُورَ","حَتَّىٰ","جَآءَ","ٱلْحَقُّ","وَظَهَرَ","أَمْرُ","ٱللَّهِ","وَهُمْ","كَٰرِهُونَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"قَلَّبَ"}},{"id":"qallaba-18-18-4","words":["verb:qallaba"],"options":[{"bs":"i okrećemo ih","en":"and we turn them over"},{"bs":"i prevrtali su","en":"and they turned over"},{"bs":"smjenjuje","en":"(He) alternates"},{"bs":"i okrećemo","en":"and we turn"}],"ref":"18:18","answerWord":"وَنُقَلِّبُهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/40b4c9147936faf836ce.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And thou wouldst have deemed them waking though they were asleep, and We caused them to turn over to the right and the left, and their dog stretching out his paws on the threshold. If thou hadst observed them closely thou hadst assuredly turned away from them in flight, and hadst been filled with awe of them.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prevrtati, okretati","en":"to turn over, to turn about"},"passage":["وَتَحْسَبُهُمْ","أَيْقَاظًا","وَهُمْ","رُقُودٌ","وَنُقَلِّبُهُمْ","ذَاتَ","ٱلْيَمِينِ","وَذَاتَ","ٱلشِّمَالِ","وَكَلْبُهُم","بَٰسِطٌ","ذِرَاعَيْهِ","بِٱلْوَصِيدِ","لَوِ","ٱطَّلَعْتَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","لَوَلَّيْتَ","مِنْهُمْ","فِرَارًا","وَلَمُلِئْتَ","مِنْهُمْ","رُعْبًا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"قَلَّبَ"}}]